prefixNestT -- SEQ 571 (Tony, 2026-11-09): stacked prefix operators nest on the NEW road (kantGrammar EXPRESSIOn), inside-out, as
many as are written, as on the old road. Rows prefixed PN-. Interpreted only (EXPRESSIOn does not run compiled yet, F-151).

One process. Each row prints three lines: "old" -- an incant/grammar action, the old road, the reference and pinned unmoved;
"top" -- STARt at the top level, new road; "act" -- an action body built through kantGrammar by compileIn with STARt (the PN RP line
proves that road: [ 7 ] is the new road's binding). r is reset to "pre" before each, so a statement that wrote nothing reads pre.
qv 3, qa 10, qb 4, x0 0, x5 5, h := nv (7). A FALSE result carries no data on both roads, so it prints r's own tag, "r": the
language's false (! x5 and x5 == 4 read alike), not a defect; PN-2 and PN-6 pin it, each paired with a non-zero sibling.

Today the new road keeps ONLY THE LAST prefix of a run. PN-7 (- - - qv) is the dispatch's three-deep row and does not discriminate
(the last prefix alone also gives -3); PN-8 and PN-9 do. PN-11 stacks a deref (* is a prefix too, remapped to deref; - to negate;
any other operator in prefix position stays itself). PN-K1..K5 are controls: a single prefix, and a prefix on a binary operand.

